# Ground combat soldiers who are not [[mechanized infantry|mechanized]], and whose role is to harass the enemy in front of the main body of infantry.
# {{lb|en|slang|archaic}} [[bedbug|Bedbugs]] or [[flea]]s.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1887|author=Andrew A. Anderson|title=Twenty-five Years in a Waggon in the Gold Regions of Africa|page=59
|passage=Our bed was a waterproof sheet on the bare stone-floors, and as the convent swarmed with fleas of all sizes, from the heavy dragoon down to the '''light infantry''', there was no fear of a sentry sleeping on his post.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1906|author=Samuel Gridley Howe|author2=Laura Elizabeth Howe Richards|title=Letters and Journals of Samuel Gridley Howe|page=109
|passage=The affair began by a skirmishing of the fleas, who acted as cavalry; then came the main body of lice, followed by the '''light infantry''' of bedbugs, to the number of forty thousand.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Callista Roy|author2=Dorothy A. Jones|title=Nursing Knowledge Development and Clinical Practice|page=46
|passage=What they dealt with in giving nursing care was in addition to the constant influx of lice, the “'''light infantry'''” of fleas, frequent harassment by droves of huge rats, earthquakes, the fickle weather of the Russian winter, {{...}}}}

